# Files that stay in the repo but should not be uploaded to Vercel.
#
# public/ is served wholesale, so anything left in it is both deployed and
# publicly reachable — even when nothing on the site links to it. These are all
# SOURCE material that has already been converted into what the site actually
# loads, so shipping them costs build time and bandwidth for no benefit.
#
# Nothing in the build imports any of these; they are raw inputs, not modules.
# Removing a line here does not break anything, it just makes the deploy larger.

# Raw frame sets for the contact sequence.
# Converted to public/contact-motion (WebP, 9 MB) by ffmpeg.
public/contact_forms/
public/contact_forms_1/

# Raw frame archives for the hero sequence.
# Converted to public/hero-motion (WebP, 6.7 MB).
public/hero_motion.zip
public/hero_motion_1.zip

# Raw frame archives for the two scrubbed camera moves in Journey.
# hero-about_anime.zip -> public/scene/bridge  (120 WebP, 15 MB) by scripts/bridge.mjs
# about_trans.zip      -> public/scene/descent (240 WebP, 11 MB, plus sm/ at 6.4 MB)
#                         by scripts/descent.mjs
public/hero-about_anime.zip
public/about_trans.zip
# contact_draft_1.zip    -> public/scene/hotline (290 WebP at 1080p, 6.5 MB, plus sm/
#                           at 1280 wide, 3.6 MB)
# red-hotline-1920x1080  -> public/scene/hotline/still.webp (50 KB)
#                           both by scripts/hotline.mjs
# contact_draft.zip is the first draft of the same shot (300 frames, 720p),
# superseded by contact_draft_1.zip and kept only as a record.
public/contact_draft_1.zip
public/contact_draft.zip
public/red-hotline-1920x1080.png
# Frames 291-300 of the first draft's 300, left over: the current set ends
# at 290 and nothing requests these.
public/scene/hotline/frame-29[1-9].webp
public/scene/hotline/frame-300.webp
public/scene/hotline/sm/frame-29[1-9].webp
public/scene/hotline/sm/frame-300.webp

# The valley the descent comes to rest on, and Projects' old background.
# Nothing loads it any more: the section shows the held frame instead, and
# the reduced-motion path uses public/scene/descent/frame-240.webp, which
# is the same picture at 48 KB. Kept in the repo because it is the source
# every grade at that end of the sequence was measured against.
public/project_bg.png

# Original project card artwork, 19.9 MB of PNG.
# Converted to public/projects/*.webp (0.6 MB, same pixels).
public/Bail_bg.png
public/BU_bg.png
public/Kine_bg.png
public/Murmur_bg.png

# The photographic sets above feed scripts/ink.mjs, which renders the themed
# ink versions the site actually loads (public/ink/, 32 MB). They stay on disk
# as the pipeline's inputs but nothing in the site references them any more.
public/hero-motion/
public/contact-motion/
public/projects/
public/light.png
public/dark.png

# Hand-supplied art at full size, before scripts/textures.mjs grades and
# resizes it into public/byobu/. Keeping the originals means a re-grade never
# needs them regenerated; shipping them would send the same pictures twice.
public/_incoming/

# Print prototypes, rendered for approval by scripts/nishiki.mjs --proto.
public/nishiki/_proto/

# Local browser-automation output.
.playwright-cli/
